# Expectation record for 08_gcc_extensions/007_extension_keyword.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 007_extension_keyword
area               = 08_gcc_extensions
description        = The __extension__ keyword suppressing pedantic rejection of an extension construct
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Each construct wrapped in __extension__ is a well-defined extension whose value is fully
initialized before use.  All arithmetic stays inside the range of its type, so no signed
overflow occurs, and every macro argument that could be evaluated more than once is a
simple object or literal without side effect.  Every property is computed twice, once from literal constants and once from
volatile-qualified storage, so the constant folder's answer cannot stand in for the
one the backend computes at run time.
No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
ext_folded_stmt=13
ext_folded_ll=1234567890123
ext_folded_typeof=26
ext_folded_ull=100
ext_folded_max=9
ext_folded_min=4
ext_folded_nested=5
ext_folded_scale=13
ext_folded_arg=10
ext_runtime_stmt=37
ext_runtime_max=11
ext_runtime_min=6
ext_runtime_ll=1000000000023
ext_runtime_scale=19
END
